---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import MockFrame from "../../components/visuals/MockFrame.astro";
---

<Layout title="Getting started — CloudGrid Handbook">
  <Section size="lg">
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="Handbook · Getting started"
      accent="emerald"
      title="Run CloudGrid in one command."
      description="The all-in-one image runs the OTLP collector, NATS, SurrealDB, storage services, BFF, and UI. Point an OTel SDK at port 4318 and refresh the UI on port 3000."
    />
  </Section>

  <Section tone="recessed">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6 reveal">
      <MockFrame title="docker-compose.yaml">
        <div class="p-5 code-surface">
          <pre class="code-block"><code><span style="color:#a78bfa">services</span>:
  <span style="color:#60a5fa">cloudgrid</span>:
    <span style="color:#a78bfa">image</span>: <span style="color:#86efac">cloudgrid/all-in-one:latest</span>
    <span style="color:#a78bfa">ports</span>:
      - <span style="color:#fbbf24">"4318:4318"</span>   <span style="color:#64748b"># OTLP HTTP ingest</span>
      - <span style="color:#fbbf24">"3000:3000"</span>   <span style="color:#64748b"># UI + GraphQL</span>
    <span style="color:#a78bfa">environment</span>:
      <span style="color:#60a5fa">CLOUDGRID_DEPLOYMENT_MODE</span>: <span style="color:#86efac">local</span>
      <span style="color:#60a5fa">CLOUDGRID_AUTH_MODE</span>: <span style="color:#86efac">local</span></code></pre>
        </div>
      </MockFrame>

      <MockFrame title="$ start">
        <div class="p-5 code-surface text-sm">
          <pre class="code-block"><code><span style="color:#86efac">$</span> docker compose up
<span style="color:#64748b">✓ NATS JetStream ready on :4222</span>
<span style="color:#64748b">✓ SurrealDB ready on :8000</span>
<span style="color:#64748b">✓ storage-write subscribed</span>
<span style="color:#64748b">✓ storage-read subscribed</span>
<span style="color:#64748b">✓ otlp-collector listening on :4318</span>
<span style="color:#64748b">✓ BFF + UI listening on :3000</span>

<span style="color:#86efac">$</span> open http://localhost:3000</code></pre>
        </div>
      </MockFrame>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <div class="prose-handbook">
      <h2>Send your first trace</h2>
      <p>
        Any OpenTelemetry SDK works. Point its OTLP HTTP exporter at
        <code>http://localhost:4318</code>. Within three seconds, the trace appears in
        <code>/traces</code>.
      </p>

      <h3>Example: TypeScript</h3>
      <p>
        Use the standard <code>@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-node</code> with the
        <code>@opentelemetry/exporter-trace-otlp-http</code> exporter. No CloudGrid SDK exists,
        and that is intentional — your existing OTel pipeline is the SDK.
      </p>

      <h3>Example: Go</h3>
      <p>
        Use <code>go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp</code>. Same
        endpoint, same wire format.
      </p>

      <h2>What now</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Explore the UI at <code>http://localhost:3000</code> — the Personal project is created automatically in local mode.</li>
        <li>Read the <a href="/handbook/architecture">Architecture page</a> to understand the message bridge.</li>
        <li>Read the <a href="/handbook/deployment">Deployment page</a> when you're ready to move beyond a laptop.</li>
        <li>Read the <a href="/handbook/configuration">Configuration page</a> for SSO and project setup.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where the contracts live</h2>
      <p>
        The OTLP ingest contract, message bridge subjects, and GraphQL schema are all defined in
        <a href="https://github.com/cloudgriddev/cloudgrid/tree/main/specs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the specs directory</a>.
        The Handbook describes them in prose; the specs are the law.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Layout>
